<<<
beware is now used only where de would be the part required with ware regarded as = cautious, i.e. in the imperative (B. of the dog!), infinitive (He had better b.), & pres. subjunctive (Unless they b.); bewaring, I beware or bewared, was bewared of, &c., are obsolete.
===
**beware** is now used only where *be* would be the part required with *ware* regarded as = cautious, i.e. in the imperative (*B. of the dog!*), infinitive (*He had better b.*), & pres. subjunctive (*Unless they b.*); *bewaring, I beware* or *bewared,* was *bewared* of, &c., are obsolete.
>>>

